From: Spike patch
Subject: [PATCH] motion: force calibration exit after 60 frames for constant-motion scenes

Frigate's ImprovedMotionDetector requires pct_motion < 5% to exit
calibration. With a looping pedestrian test clip this condition is never
met (constant motion), so detection_fps stays 0 forever.

Fix: also exit calibration when frame_counter reaches 60 (12 s at 5 fps).
The background model has already converged via the alpha=0.2 fast-update
path; forcing calibration exit lets the existing motion boxes reach the
object detector. The lightning_threshold guard still protects against true
scene-change storms.

Spike-only patch -- production Frigate cameras are static with natural
quiet intervals; this code path is only a problem for looping test clips.

--- a/frigate/motion/improved_motion.py
+++ b/frigate/motion/improved_motion.py
@@ -178,7 +178,10 @@ class ImprovedMotionDetector(MotionDetector):

-        # once the motion is less than 5% and the number of contours is < 4, assume its calibrated
-        if pct_motion < 0.05 and len(motion_boxes) <= 4:
+        # once the motion is less than 5% and the number of contours is < 4,
+        # assume its calibrated; also force exit after 60 frames so constant-
+        # motion scenes (looping test clips) can still reach the object detector.
+        if (pct_motion < 0.05 and len(motion_boxes) <= 4) or self.frame_counter >= 60:
             self.calibrating = False

